{{also|Tyo|tyó}}
==Finnish==
{{Finnish index|t|y}}

===Pronunciation===
{{fi-pronunciation}}

===Etymology 1===
From {{inh|fi|fiu-fin-pro|*töö}}, from {{inh|fi|fiu-pro|*tewe}}; cognate with {{cog|et|-}} and {{cog|vot|töö}} and {{cog|liv|tīe}}.

====Noun====
{{fi-noun}}

# [[work]] {{gloss|labour, employment, occupation, job}}
# work {{gloss|effort expended on a particular task}}
# work {{gloss|physics: mechanics and thermodynamics}}
# work {{gloss|artistic or intellectual production}}
# work {{gloss|place of work}}
# [[job]]

=====Usage notes=====
When saying "at work", "to work" or "from work", the locational cases are used in plural.
:{{uxi|fi|Olen '''töissä'''.|I am at '''work'''.}}
:{{uxi|fi|mennä '''töihin'''|go to '''work'''}}

=====Declension=====
{{fi-decl-suo|työ|ä}}

=====Synonyms=====
* {{sense|job}} {{l|fi|duuni}} {{qualifier|slang, colloquial}}
* {{sense|artistic or intellectual production}} {{l|fi|teos}}
* {{sense|place of work}} {{l|fi|työpaikka}}; {{l|fi|duuni}} {{qualifier|slang, colloquial}}

